secubox-torrent (2.2.4-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=high

  * PERF FIX (event-loop peg / board-wide slowdown / torrent 503): the engine
    kept every streamed torrent loaded and SEEDED completed movies to peers with
    no upload cap, pegging the single JS event loop at 100% CPU for hours.
    We are a viewing SAS, NOT a seedbox:
    - upload is capped at HALF the live download bandwidth, and drops to 0 once a
      torrent is 100% (tuneUpload every 5s) — no seeding of finished content;
    - maxConns capped (default 20);
    - idle torrents are unloaded from the engine after 15min (data kept) —
      transit-lounge model. TORRENT_SEED=full re-enables real seeding.
  * rename app entry server.js -> webtorrent-server.js (clarity).

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 17:30:00 +0200

