secubox-torrent (2.2.1-1~bookworm1) bookworm; urgency=high

  * Fix "Bad Request" on keep/remove/conserve: the panel sent
    Content-Type: application/json with no body, which Fastify 400s
    (FST_ERR_CTP_EMPTY_JSON_BODY). The webui now only sets that header when it
    sends a body, and the server tolerates an empty json body.
  * Fix "les torrents ne repartent pas": incomplete downloads now RESUME after a
    restart. A `complete` flag (set on the WebTorrent 'done' event, kept in sync
    on /list) lets resumeLibrary re-add ONLY still-downloading torrents (complete
    ones stay lazy — no boot re-hash storm). New POST /resume/<ih> +  a
    "▶ Reprendre" panel button loads/resumes a lazy torrent on demand and
    corrects its flag (covers torrents from before the flag existed). Migration
    marks pre-existing rows complete=1 (no storm); use ▶ Reprendre once to
    resume an old unfinished download.

 -- Gerald KERMA <devel@cybermind.fr>  Wed, 30 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0200

